atial references</h1></header><div id=3D"skip-to-content" class=3D"afd-flow=
-content page-content"><p>A spatial reference is a characteristic of a geom=
etry that identifies how its coordinates relate to real-world space. It is =
important for ensuring that spatial data in different layers, graphic overl=
ays, and feature sets can be used together for accurate viewing or analysis=
.</p><p>Spatial references can be referred to by a well-known ID (WKID)=E2=
=80=94an integer value. Some common WKIDs are mentioned in the text below; =
for a more complete description, see <a href=3D"https://developers.arcgis.c=
om/qt/spatial-and-data-analysis/spatial-references/#spatial-reference-speci=
fications">Spatial reference specifications</a> in this topic.</p>
