<p>Datum transformations are used when geometries must be projected from on=
e spatial reference to another when there is a difference in the datum that=
 underlies the two spatial references. The following transformations are su=
pported:</p><ul>
<li><a href=3D"https://developers.arcgis.com/qt/spatial-and-data-analysis/s=
patial-references/#horizontal-and-vertical-transformations">Horizontal (geo=
graphic) and vertical datum transformations</a></li>
<li>Ellipsoidal and <a href=3D"https://developers.arcgis.com/qt/spatial-and=
-data-analysis/spatial-references/#grid-based-transformations">grid-based t=
ransformations</a></li>
</ul><p>As a developer, you can:</p><ul>
<li>Obtain the default transformation for the projection.</li>
<li>Customize the default transformation used by your app through a JSON co=
nfiguration file.</li>
<li>Consider the best transformation for a specific work area.</li>
<li>Choose from a list of suitable transformations from the transformation =
catalog for a given pair of spatial references and optionally a given geogr=
aphic area.</li>
<li>Create a transformation using WKIDs.</li>
<li>Create a custom transformation using WKT, if you have even more special=
ized needs.</li>
</ul><h3 id=3D"horizontal-and-vertical-transformations" class=3D"group rela=
tive">Horizontal and vertical transformations<a href=3D"https://developers.=
arcgis.com/qt/spatial-and-data-analysis/spatial-references/#horizontal-and-=
vertical-transformations" aria-label=3D"horizontal and vertical transformat=
ions permalink" tabindex=3D"0" class=3D"anchor-link"><span><svg xmlns=3D"ht=
tp://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height=3D"16" width=3D"16" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16">=
<path d=3D"M5 9.5a4.505 4.505 0 0 0 .048.493c-.007-.007-.016-.011-.023-.018=
l-3-3a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95-4.95l3 3a3.486 3.486 0 0 1-1.31 5.76l-.226-.225a1.=
484 1.484 0 0 1-.37-.631 2.495 2.495 0 0 0 1.199-4.197l-3-3a2.5 2.5 0 1 0-3=
.536 3.536L5.09 8.625A4.498 4.498 0 0 0 5 9.5zm11 3a3.475 3.475 0 0 0-1.025=
-2.475l-3-3c-.007-.007-.016-.011-.023-.018A4.505 4.505 0 0 1 12 7.5a4.498 4=
