3.527-.008l-3-3a2.5 2.5 0 0 1-.094-3.436 2.43 2.43 0 0 1 1.3-.74 1.485 1.48=
5 0 0 0-.377-.652l-.222-.222a3.482 3.482 0 0 0-1.314 5.757l3 3a3.5 3.5 0 0 =
0 4.937.012l-.351-.355.352.355A3.476 3.476 0 0 0 16 12.5z"></path><path fil=
l=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h16v16H0z"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>Exactly how =
coordinates should be transformed is defined by agencies such as the US Nat=
ional Geodetic Survey. Esri's Projection Engine supports many predefined tr=
ansformations, and more than one transformation may be available for a give=
n datum change. Each transformation is identified by a WKID integer number =
and WKT text string definition, similarly to how spatial references are ide=
ntified. Transformations vary in accuracy, and using the most suitable tran=
sformation for your specific case ensures the best possible accuracy for th=
e reprojection.</p><p>Geographic transformations translate horizontal (x,y)=
 coordinates from the <a href=3D"https://developers.arcgis.com/qt/spatial-a=
nd-data-analysis/spatial-references/#coordinate-systems-and-projections">ge=
ographic coordinate system</a> of the input spatial reference to the geogra=
phic coordinate system of the output spatial reference, accounting for the =
difference in geographic (horizontal) datum. For spatial references with a =
<a href=3D"https://developers.arcgis.com/qt/spatial-and-data-analysis/spati=
al-references/#coordinate-systems-and-projections">vertical coordinate syst=
em</a> set, vertical transformations translate vertical positions (z-values=
) from one vertical coordinate system to another, accounting for the differ=
ence in vertical datum. Horizontal and vertical transformations can be used=
 together if there is a change in both datums.</p><p>Each of the supported =
predefined transformations and is represented by one or more steps (the <co=
de>Geographic<wbr>Transformation<wbr>Step</code> or <code>Horizontal<wbr>Ve=
rtical<wbr>Transformation<wbr>Step</code> type) in a transformation (the <c=
ode>Geographic<wbr>Transformation</code> or <code>Horizontal<wbr>Vertical<w=
br>Transformation</code> type).</p><h3 id=3D"grid-based-transformations" cl=
ass=3D"group relative">Grid-based transformations<a href=3D"https://develop=
